# What `notify` has already reported, so a scheduled pass only tells you
# about conditions that are new. Per-machine and disposable:
# delete it and the next pass reports the current backlog again.
.archimedes-notify.json

# The runs archimedes had under way, one directory each, holding the
# snapshot that would put a target repo back if a run died before it could.
# Per-machine and about repos elsewhere on this machine, so it is no more
# this instance's history than the file above: `unfinished-runs`
# is what reads them, and a run that ends well takes its own away.
.archimedes-runs/
